WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:01.000
{Chapter 07}

00:08.530 --> 00:10.070
Bring it, Takumi.

00:17.120 --> 00:21.210
You don't need to bring the
ball to me every time, stupid.

00:23.000 --> 00:25.459
That was awesome!

00:25.460 --> 00:27.469
It was like whoosh, bam,

00:27.470 --> 00:30.219
and the ball's in my hand.

00:30.220 --> 00:33.219
Stop being so overly dramatic.

00:33.220 --> 00:35.309
I don't know how to put it.

00:35.310 --> 00:38.729
I just get excited
when I think it's coming.

00:38.730 --> 00:39.730
And then...

00:39.731 --> 00:41.729
All right, I get it.

00:41.730 --> 00:44.769
But you can't come
tell me after every pitch.

00:44.770 --> 00:45.819
Hurry up and get back there.

00:45.820 --> 00:47.070
Okay, okay.

00:58.580 --> 01:00.959
Hey, let's call it a day.

01:00.960 --> 01:02.170
Okay.

01:04.340 --> 01:07.210
You're going to apply to
the team tomorrow, right?

01:08.170 --> 01:09.170
Yeah.

01:16.930 --> 01:22.190
Takumi, do you plan on
mastering some breaking balls?

01:24.310 --> 01:26.479
My grandpa said something to me before.

01:26.480 --> 01:30.190
He said not to even throw curveballs
while I'm using the soft baseballs.

01:30.820 --> 01:33.159
Yeah, fastballs are probably good enough.

01:33.160 --> 01:35.950
It'll be plenty effective
for junior-high baseball.

01:36.530 --> 01:38.410
I wouldn't rely on breaking balls,

01:39.330 --> 01:43.920
but I'm going to master them
when my body's finished developing.

01:45.130 --> 01:46.880
You plan on that too.

02:05.190 --> 02:10.740
I've heard it said so many times

02:11.440 --> 02:17.660
How it's not going to work out

02:18.620 --> 02:24.120
That nothing will change

02:24.420 --> 02:30.630
Even if I pretended not to listen

02:31.090 --> 02:34.469
I knew it all

02:34.470 --> 02:37.639
I learned this from you

02:37.640 --> 02:45.640
That it's not a failure, even when it is

02:47.020 --> 02:53.609
When I thrust my feelings
on to the drifting clouds

02:53.610 --> 03:00.529
The quiet melodies push me forward

03:00.530 --> 03:07.039
Because the sky is so vast and free

03:07.040 --> 03:14.670
I decided that I wouldn't cry anymore

03:22.810 --> 03:25.809
This is the flavor from his
childhood he just described.

03:25.810 --> 03:28.309
It's his mother's kinpira gobo.

03:28.310 --> 03:31.189
Yes, this is it.

03:31.190 --> 03:32.320
This really takes me back.

03:34.990 --> 03:35.990
What?

03:36.530 --> 03:37.739
I'm applying for the team.

03:37.740 --> 03:41.120
Write your name down where it
says "guardian" sometime today.

03:41.830 --> 03:44.829
Hold on just a second.
What's with your attitude?

03:44.830 --> 03:48.210
Why are you always ordering people around?

03:48.920 --> 03:50.629
That wasn't an order.

03:50.630 --> 03:52.710
So that's how you ask someone for a favor?

03:53.000 --> 03:54.170
I didn't ask for a favor.

03:55.090 --> 03:57.469
I decided to join the baseball team.

03:57.470 --> 03:59.549
I know that.

03:59.550 --> 04:01.719
I would never suggest it to you.

04:01.720 --> 04:04.349
Makiko, just leave it alone.

04:04.350 --> 04:07.809
Why are you so irritated when
he's just applying for the team?

04:07.810 --> 04:09.479
Stay out of this, Dad!

04:09.480 --> 04:11.730
He's always like this!

04:12.310 --> 04:15.729
What would you do if I said I was
against you joining the baseball team?

04:15.730 --> 04:18.530
It doesn't matter if you're against it.

04:19.450 --> 04:22.319
Yes, of course. I thought you'd say that.

04:22.320 --> 04:23.320
But...

04:23.830 --> 04:26.829
who do you think has to
wash your muddy uniform?

04:26.830 --> 04:29.750
Who do you think has to pack
you a lunch for your games?

04:30.580 --> 04:35.050
I don't think it's unreasonable for you to
realize there are people supporting you.

04:45.720 --> 04:48.810
<i>I'm going to master them when
my body's finished developing.</i>

04:49.770 --> 04:51.560
<i>You plan on that too.</i>

04:58.690 --> 05:01.950
Maybe I'll just quit baseball.

05:08.040 --> 05:13.040
So then I'd just watch him form
a battery with someone else?

05:14.790 --> 05:19.010
Why'd I have to meet a guy like Takumi?

05:36.730 --> 05:38.650
You there. Your button.

05:39.440 --> 05:42.950
Your collar is unbuttoned.

05:44.450 --> 05:45.530
What's your name and class?

05:46.490 --> 05:47.490
Let go!

05:51.710 --> 05:52.710
Come with me.

05:55.670 --> 05:57.170
Faculty Office

05:56.630 --> 05:58.670
Harada Takumi?

05:59.340 --> 06:00.879
That's a good name.

06:00.880 --> 06:03.300
You've got a good look in your eyes.

06:04.180 --> 06:06.509
Do I? Thank you.

06:06.510 --> 06:08.849
So, what do you have?

06:08.850 --> 06:09.680
Huh?

06:09.681 --> 06:13.140
In your pocket. I'm
asking what's inside it.

06:15.310 --> 06:16.310
A Tokarev.

06:18.230 --> 06:19.570
Answer me seriously.

06:24.070 --> 06:26.200
Nice Tokarev.

06:26.780 --> 06:30.700
But you shouldn't bring anything
that isn't school-related here.

06:31.160 --> 06:33.210
It <i>is</i> school-related.

06:35.040 --> 06:36.960
Show me your hand.

06:47.890 --> 06:49.970
Take off your jacket.

07:05.900 --> 07:08.530
You've got good musculature.

07:10.490 --> 07:13.450
How much running do you do?

07:14.540 --> 07:16.669
About 5 or 6 kilometers a day.

07:16.670 --> 07:19.669
And you make sure to stretch, I bet.

07:19.670 --> 07:22.499
Yet you still can't pitch a breaking ball.

07:22.500 --> 07:24.589
Is that about right, Harada?

07:24.590 --> 07:26.180
That's about right.

07:27.010 --> 07:29.179
Who's training you?

07:29.180 --> 07:30.299
Nobody.

07:30.300 --> 07:34.059
You can't tell me you don't
have any baseball experience.

07:34.060 --> 07:37.139
I was on a Little League team.

07:37.140 --> 07:41.439
But I did the running on my own.

07:41.440 --> 07:45.779
That's quite an attitude
you have for a freshman.

07:45.780 --> 07:47.450
You could show some remorse.

07:47.990 --> 07:49.489
Please give me back my baseball.

07:49.490 --> 07:55.700
All non-scholastic items are
confiscated for being against the rules.

07:56.040 --> 07:57.409
Please give it back.

07:57.410 --> 07:58.710
It does matter to me.

08:06.260 --> 08:08.009
So you're applying to the team?

08:08.010 --> 08:10.260
You sure took your time.

08:10.550 --> 08:16.179
You think you can have the ball since you're
joining the baseball team, is that it?

08:16.180 --> 08:17.180
Yes.

08:17.810 --> 08:21.440
Well, that kind of argument's
not gonna work here.

08:22.820 --> 08:24.860
Never take that out of your pocket.

08:25.400 --> 08:27.610
And don't play catch in the hallways.

08:28.360 --> 08:30.409
What's so funny?

08:30.410 --> 08:33.370
Who would play catch in the hallways?

08:33.700 --> 08:35.289
Hey, it happens sometimes.

08:35.290 --> 08:39.120
Some idiots break windows by
throwing a ball around in the hallway.

08:40.000 --> 08:43.209
I'm sure you could if you're
just tossing the ball around.

08:43.210 --> 08:45.130
But playing catch isn't just for fun.

08:48.470 --> 08:52.340
It's not often you meet
such an argumentative guy.

08:53.180 --> 08:55.260
All right, get back to your classroom.

08:56.640 --> 08:57.640
Thank you.

09:08.530 --> 09:09.530
Takumi.

09:17.040 --> 09:18.040
Yo.

09:18.041 --> 09:21.329
I heard you got pulled
into the faculty office.

09:21.330 --> 09:25.039
So I came to check on you,
and I see you just grinning.

09:25.040 --> 09:27.379
Me? Grinning?

09:27.380 --> 09:28.629
Yep.

09:28.630 --> 09:30.759
That's the famous Harada for you.

09:30.760 --> 09:33.009
Otomurai gave you a lecture, didn't he?

09:33.010 --> 09:36.390
Yet you're still grinning.
I guess I have nothing to worry about.

09:37.180 --> 09:38.180
Otomurai?

09:38.890 --> 09:40.179
That's right.

09:40.180 --> 09:42.139
That's Mr. Tomura's nickname.

09:42.140 --> 09:44.400
He's the baseball coach.

09:51.820 --> 09:54.819
That guy's strangely gloomy.

09:54.820 --> 09:56.909
I wouldn't go that far.

09:56.910 --> 10:00.329
But I wouldn't say the vice
captain is very cheerful either.

10:00.330 --> 10:01.660
Vice captain?

10:02.370 --> 10:04.539
Not of the baseball team, I hope.

10:04.540 --> 10:05.880
Yes, of the baseball team.

10:06.630 --> 10:09.299
That's Nobunishi. He
plays catcher and bats third.

10:09.300 --> 10:10.550
Seriously?

10:20.430 --> 10:21.809
Mr. Kusanagi.

10:21.810 --> 10:23.019
Yes?

10:23.020 --> 10:26.649
Could I take a look at the student
questionnaire for your class?

10:26.650 --> 10:28.190
Of course.

10:30.690 --> 10:31.780
Here it is.

10:32.320 --> 10:33.695
Harada Takumi

10:32.320 --> 10:33.695
Nitta East Junior High

10:32.320 --> 10:35.069
None

10:33.696 --> 10:35.070
Male

10:33.696 --> 10:35.070
Class 2

10:35.070 --> 10:39.660
He's barely filled
anything out about himself.

10:40.330 --> 10:43.619
Hobbies, talents, best subjects...

10:43.620 --> 10:46.629
He doesn't even have the most
important part, his list of friends.

10:46.630 --> 10:47.580
Hm?

10:47.580 --> 10:49.085
Father

10:47.580 --> 10:49.085
Office Worker

10:47.580 --> 10:49.085
Harada Makiko

10:47.580 --> 10:49.085
Mother

10:47.580 --> 10:49.085
Harada Seiha

10:47.580 --> 10:49.085
Brother

10:47.580 --> 10:49.085
Ioka Youzou

10:47.580 --> 10:49.085
Grandfather

10:47.580 --> 10:49.085
Family

10:47.580 --> 10:49.085
Name

10:47.580 --> 10:49.085
Relation

10:47.580 --> 10:49.085
Occupation

10:47.581 --> 10:49.085
Harada Hiroshi

10:48.380 --> 10:49.960
Coach Ioka?

10:50.920 --> 10:53.009
Coach Ioka?

10:53.010 --> 10:56.589
As in the Ioka who used to
coach Nitta High's baseball team?

10:56.590 --> 10:57.639
That's right.

10:57.640 --> 11:00.350
Apparently that boy from
earlier is his grandson.

11:00.640 --> 11:05.439
That's right, you played for Nitta
High's baseball team, didn't you?

11:05.440 --> 11:08.149
Were you coached by Ioka?

11:08.150 --> 11:14.360
Yeah, but when I was a
junior, he suddenly quit.

11:14.700 --> 11:17.990
We weren't much of a team after.

11:18.870 --> 11:19.490
One, two.

11:19.490 --> 11:20.200
Oh, yeah.

11:20.200 --> 11:20.870
One, two.

11:20.870 --> 11:21.540
Oh, yeah.

11:21.540 --> 11:22.240
One, two.

11:22.240 --> 11:22.910
Oh, yeah.

11:22.910 --> 11:23.620
One, two.

11:23.620 --> 11:24.250
Oh, yeah.

11:24.250 --> 11:24.960
One, two.

11:24.960 --> 11:25.960
Oh, yeah.

11:35.720 --> 11:37.180
Gather up.

11:42.760 --> 11:44.560
That's the captain, Kaionji.

11:45.640 --> 11:49.650
All right, we'll be starting real
batting drills today like we discussed.

11:50.190 --> 11:52.189
We'll be dividing you up into two groups.

11:52.190 --> 11:54.739
Freshmen will be
gathering balls in the outfield.

11:54.740 --> 11:58.160
There'll be no chatting
or sitting down to rest.

11:58.820 --> 12:00.659
Anything else, Coach?

12:00.660 --> 12:03.659
Sounds good for practice.

12:03.660 --> 12:05.949
Just one thing before we start.

12:05.950 --> 12:06.950
Harada.

12:07.210 --> 12:08.210
Yes, sir.

12:08.420 --> 12:09.750
Go to the mound.

12:11.880 --> 12:13.169
Quiet.

12:13.170 --> 12:16.170
I'll let anyone else who wants
to pitch have a chance too.

12:16.510 --> 12:18.680
But Harada goes first.

12:19.130 --> 12:21.430
Nobunishi, catch for him.

12:22.010 --> 12:23.010
Yes, sir.

12:23.970 --> 12:25.810
Good luck, Takumi.

12:33.770 --> 12:36.230
All right, go ahead and pitch, Harada.

12:40.490 --> 12:41.660
He needs to wear protection.

12:47.290 --> 12:48.410
Oh?

13:08.890 --> 13:11.520
Harada, hurry up.

13:20.490 --> 13:21.490
Hey.

13:22.910 --> 13:24.240
Is he okay?

13:27.740 --> 13:30.120
I'm sorry. My hand slipped.

13:33.170 --> 13:35.999
Coach, I think I need
to take a little break.

13:36.000 --> 13:38.050
Yeah, better safe than sorry.

13:40.590 --> 13:44.090
In that case, I'll catch instead.

13:45.350 --> 13:46.350
Coach.

13:48.060 --> 13:52.349
Would it be okay for me to
pick a catcher I work well with?

13:52.350 --> 13:54.099
Hey, Gou.

13:54.100 --> 13:58.069
Do you think Harada threw that ball
wild on purpose to get you out there?

13:58.070 --> 14:00.109
No way. Don't be stupid.

14:00.110 --> 14:02.319
But I just thought...

14:02.320 --> 14:04.739
Even if you think it,
don't say it out loud.

14:04.740 --> 14:06.239
Don't tell Sawa either.

14:06.240 --> 14:07.449
Nagakura.

14:07.450 --> 14:08.490
Yes, sir.

14:08.830 --> 14:10.579
You've been chosen by Harada.

14:10.580 --> 14:12.249
Come switch with Nobunishi.

14:12.250 --> 14:13.329
Yes, sir.

14:13.330 --> 14:15.880
Could I borrow some protective gear?

14:24.430 --> 14:25.930
I'm ready.

14:27.640 --> 14:28.640
Takumi.

14:31.850 --> 14:33.100
Let's do it, Gou.

14:33.810 --> 14:36.310
This is our junior-high baseball debut.

14:38.270 --> 14:39.270
Yeah.

14:39.730 --> 14:41.570
You'd better go all-out from the start.

14:42.900 --> 14:43.900
Of course.

15:10.720 --> 15:12.930
Try pitching it to the same spot again.

15:19.730 --> 15:22.939
Kaionji, get in the batter's box.

15:22.940 --> 15:23.940
Am I hitting it?

15:23.941 --> 15:25.069
You don't have to.

15:25.070 --> 15:26.430
Just act like you're about to hit.

15:28.950 --> 15:30.329
Timeout!

15:30.330 --> 15:32.619
You're on fire, dude!

15:32.620 --> 15:34.449
You're throwing some real heaters!

15:34.450 --> 15:37.119
Did you come here just to tell me that?

15:37.120 --> 15:38.120
No.

15:38.330 --> 15:41.249
I'm going to start telling
you where I want it.

15:41.250 --> 15:42.250
Don't miss.

16:06.950 --> 16:09.700
Nice one, Takumi. That was awesome!

16:16.830 --> 16:19.000
All right, that's enough.

16:19.710 --> 16:21.210
Yes, sir.

16:22.960 --> 16:24.960
I got the gist of it.

16:25.380 --> 16:27.879
You two get to the
outfield and pick up balls.

16:27.880 --> 16:28.550
But...

16:28.551 --> 16:30.719
Don't get carried away, Nagakura.

16:30.720 --> 16:33.509
You guys are still freshmen.

16:33.510 --> 16:35.970
Just do as you're told, got it?

16:36.850 --> 16:41.980
Honestly, we've got some
cheeky freshmen this year.

16:43.610 --> 16:45.940
Is there anyone else
who wants to try to pitch?

16:47.400 --> 16:50.699
All right, we're starting
the batting drills, then.

16:50.700 --> 16:52.990
Harada, come here for a sec.

16:55.240 --> 16:58.250
You should try throwing
it a little less hard.

16:58.660 --> 17:01.749
You shouldn't be
pitching all-out at your age.

17:01.750 --> 17:07.509
You need to focus on strengthening
your legs and building up your stamina.

17:07.510 --> 17:08.629
Understood.

17:08.630 --> 17:11.219
Good to hear you understand, Harada.

17:11.220 --> 17:14.010
If only you were always like this.

17:14.470 --> 17:17.519
There's no doubt you'll
become a good pitcher.

17:17.520 --> 17:22.270
But if you don't polish your
talent, you won't get very far.

17:22.770 --> 17:23.979
You got that?

17:23.980 --> 17:24.980
Yes, sir.

17:25.270 --> 17:26.609
Very good.

17:26.610 --> 17:28.280
Now, let's start with this.

17:29.650 --> 17:33.159
Your hair is too long for baseball.

17:33.160 --> 17:35.410
Go get it cut!

17:38.660 --> 17:41.410
Will cutting my hair build up my stamina?

17:42.250 --> 17:43.669
What did you say?

17:43.670 --> 17:46.670
The things you just talked
about make sense to me.

17:47.170 --> 17:49.759
What does it matter how long my hair is?

17:49.760 --> 17:51.680
Just do as you're told!

17:52.260 --> 17:54.679
I will regarding my practice regimen.

17:54.680 --> 17:57.929
Why is your attitude so awful, you fool?!

17:57.930 --> 18:00.099
It's because you're being unreasonable.

18:00.100 --> 18:01.690
How am I being unreasonable?

18:02.140 --> 18:06.440
Please don't bring up my hair length
when it has nothing to do with baseball.

18:06.900 --> 18:08.780
It doesn't make sense at all.

18:11.360 --> 18:14.359
Go get your hair cut. I want you bald.

18:14.360 --> 18:16.530
Fix your appearance.

18:17.200 --> 18:20.950
We're ready for the drills, sir.

18:21.910 --> 18:22.910
Okay.

18:25.130 --> 18:26.500
Go to the outfield.

18:30.590 --> 18:32.379
Man, practice is tough.

18:32.380 --> 18:34.339
Yeah.

18:34.340 --> 18:36.469
Otomurai was so scary.

18:36.470 --> 18:38.100
He wasn't that bad.

18:40.770 --> 18:43.889
Takumi, are you really not
going to get your hair cut?

18:43.890 --> 18:44.890
No way.

18:46.270 --> 18:47.809
But...

18:47.810 --> 18:49.860
You worry too much.

18:50.480 --> 18:53.859
Idiot. What good will
disobeying the coach do you?

18:53.860 --> 18:55.489
Yeah, Harada.

18:55.490 --> 18:59.079
If you disobey the coach,
he won't let you play.

18:59.080 --> 19:01.620
You'd be a starter in no time.

19:01.950 --> 19:06.709
Seems our team has had weak
pitchers, so this is a big break for you.

19:06.710 --> 19:08.749
Yeah, just play ball here.

19:08.750 --> 19:09.750
No way.

19:10.670 --> 19:13.299
Hey, hold on. This really
could be your big break.

19:13.300 --> 19:15.380
Stop screwing around, stupid!

19:15.800 --> 19:18.639
I'm not stupid, and I'm
not screwing around either.

19:18.640 --> 19:20.139
I'm serious.

19:20.140 --> 19:22.679
You're stupid because you're being serious.

19:22.680 --> 19:28.149
There's no way I'm letting
Otomurai make me cut my hair.

19:28.150 --> 19:33.279
You say that, but what if he
doesn't put you in the game?

19:33.280 --> 19:37.070
You don't let someone put
you in games, you just play.

19:37.780 --> 19:43.539
I imagine Otomurai wants to make it
to the prefectural finals and nationals.

19:43.540 --> 19:48.209
You mean he'll have to
use you if he wants to win?

19:48.210 --> 19:49.290
Basically.

19:50.840 --> 19:52.300
But, Harada,

19:52.750 --> 19:55.759
what if Otomurai doesn't
care about winning?

19:55.760 --> 19:57.299
What do you mean?

19:57.300 --> 20:03.889
If you keep mouthing off, he might
rather lose than give in and let you play.

20:03.890 --> 20:11.560
Yeah, what are you going to do if he doesn't put you
in the game because he says you disrupt teamwork?

20:12.190 --> 20:13.689
Then I won't play.

20:13.690 --> 20:14.690
What?

20:14.691 --> 20:16.400
I don't need to play.

20:17.570 --> 20:19.199
What do you mean, you don't need to play?

20:19.200 --> 20:21.989
We're not just talking about this year.

20:21.990 --> 20:23.909
He might not let you
play next year, either.

20:23.910 --> 20:24.989
That's fine.

20:24.990 --> 20:28.920
I'd rather not play than have
to do everything he tells me.

20:29.710 --> 20:30.830
Are you kidding me?!

20:31.840 --> 20:34.089
What do you mean, you
don't give a shit if you play?!

20:34.090 --> 20:34.840
Gou!

20:34.841 --> 20:36.089
Stop it, Gou!

20:36.090 --> 20:39.089
Why don't you stop looking
down on everyone all the time?!

20:39.090 --> 20:41.589
Stop, Gou! You'll kill him!

20:41.590 --> 20:43.100
Let go of him!

20:54.110 --> 20:55.230
You're...

20:57.070 --> 20:58.190
the worst kind of person.

21:27.270 --> 21:31.815
I saw you running after
a sparkling white ball

21:31.816 --> 21:36.359
I saw you running after
a sparkling white ball

21:36.360 --> 21:41.865
As it followed a parabola,
disappearing into distant memories

21:41.866 --> 21:47.370
As it followed a parabola,
disappearing into distant memories

21:49.910 --> 21:54.415
You looked back as you
chased after it from afar

21:54.416 --> 21:58.919
You looked back as you
chased after it from afar

